WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.920
We all know how tough it can be to get through
a standard work day when we're dealing with

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.979
tough personal circumstances.

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:09.790
Many of your favorite actors may have dealt
with dark nights of the soul while still showing

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:14.760
up to work every day, only in their cases,
the record is there for all to see.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:20.480
Since 2009, Reid Ewing has appeared on the
ABC sitcom Modern Family as Haley's boyfriend

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.490
Dylan.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:25.350
He landed the role at 21, when he was struggling
with what he now knows to be a body dysmorphia

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.350
disorder.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.710
Since his early teens, the handsome actor
hasn't been able to look in a mirror without

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.930
seeing a horribly ugly person staring back.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.880
Ewing had his first plastic surgery at the
age of 19.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.840
More procedures followed, each one causing
a new perceived problem that he felt could

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.200
only be fixed by more surgery.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.030
He eventually sought help after experiencing
suicidal depression in 2012.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:50.340
With the aid of therapy and medication, he's
come to understand his disorder while working

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.300
as an advocate for those suffering from it.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.501
"And I remember looking at that photo, and
that was the moment where I said I had to

00:00:56.501 --> 00:01:00.800
get, you know, cosmetic surgery because, like,
no one was allowed to be that ugly."

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.520
Irish actor Devon Murray had the luck, or
perhaps misfortune, of beginning his career

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.400
with a role in one of the most beloved film
franchises of all time.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.000
At 11 years old, he was cast as Seamus Finnegan
in Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.430
a role he'd reprise in all eight films in
the series.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.180
This might seem like a dream gig, but the
prolonged periods of separation from his friends

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.710
and family in Ireland eventually took a toll
on the young star.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.790
In an interview with Irish National Broadcaster
RTE, Murray elaborated:

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:33.360
"It was my 16th birthday and I was staying
in this fantastic hotel suite over in London

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.250
and my room was full of presents from everybody
and I should have been happy but I wasn't."

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.150
Murray struggled with depression, and he very
nearly committed suicide in early 2016.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:47.460
He sought help at the urging of family, and
has since spoken publicly about his experiences.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.570
Team America: World Police is perhaps Trey
Parker and Matt Stone's greatest film, a hilarious

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:56.030
satire of both action movies and American
foreign policy.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.270
It's a pretty remarkable achievement, especially
considering that it nearly destroyed the lives

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.710
and partnership of its creators.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.140
Stone famously vowed to never make another
movie with puppets or Parker again, so toxic

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.269
was their working relationship on the film.

00:02:09.269 --> 00:02:13.819
South Park is still going strong over a decade
later, but Stone has remained true to his

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:14.819
word.

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:18.329
The duo have never made another film together,
and even though the world is just screaming

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:22.669
for a Team America sequel right about now,
it's unlikely in the extreme that we'll get

00:02:22.669 --> 00:02:23.160
one.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.280
The fatal overdose of River Phoenix in 1993
instantly cut short what was almost certain

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.040
to be a long and important acting career.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.829
The 23-year old was the definition of a hot
rising star, not to mention a prodigally gifted

00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:38.849
actor, and few of his friends were hit harder
than Keanu Reeves.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:43.230
Reeves, who had been close friends with Phoenix
for years and co-starred with him in My Own

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:47.169
Private Idaho, was at work on the set of Speed
when he received the news.

00:02:47.169 --> 00:02:51.579
Phoenix had developed his lethal drug addiction
during the filming of Private Idaho, a role

00:02:51.579 --> 00:02:53.739
Reeves had persuaded him to take.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:56.629
The production of Speed was nearly shut down
completely.

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:00.639
But it restarted after a short break, with
cast and crew giving Reeves plenty of space

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.700
and consideration as he dealt with his grief.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.859
The filming of Francis Ford Coppola's 1979
Vietnam War masterpiece Apocalypse Now was

00:03:08.859 --> 00:03:11.939
legendarily taxing on everybody involved.

00:03:11.939 --> 00:03:16.980
Coppola pushed cast and crew alike to their
absolute limits, none more so than star Martin

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:17.980
Sheen.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.620
For one infamous scene in a hotel room early
in the film, Sheen was kept drunk for two

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.939
days while being goaded mercilessly by Coppola.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:30.370
The actor became sick and lost weight, and
during a break from filming, he openly admitted

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.510
to friends that he wasn't sure if he'd survive
the shoot.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.670
He finished the film having had a heart attack
and a nervous breakdown, and at one point

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:41.400
he was so ill that a local priest administered
last rites.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.500
The late, great Robin Williams is a case study
in how the funniest and most engaging people

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:50.260
can still struggle with serious physical and
mental health issues.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.979
The actor dealt with depression for much of
his career while working constantly, and he

00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:59.120
ended his own life in 2014 at the age of 63
after a prolonged battle with a degenerative

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.799
brain disorder called Lewy's body dementia.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:06.209
It's likely that evidence of Williams' struggles
could be found in a great deal of his body

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:10.169
of work, but one example late in his career
stands out.

00:04:10.169 --> 00:04:14.589
Released the year of his death, The Angriest
Man in Brooklyn tells the story of a perpetually

00:04:14.589 --> 00:04:19.099
raging New Yorker given 90 minutes to live
after a brain aneurysm.

00:04:19.099 --> 00:04:23.669
At one point, he goes on an extended rant
about the meaninglessness and injustice of

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:27.770
life, and cinematographer John Bailey was
taken aback while filming the scene.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:31.849
He called the performance a glimpse into the
"Swiftian darkness of Robin's heart," and

00:04:31.849 --> 00:04:35.050
went so far as to call it his defining role.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:38.949
If you're struggling with suicidal thoughts,
please call the National Suicide Prevention

00:04:38.949 --> 00:04:42.800
Lifeline at 1-800-273-8255.

